        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_8e7577771da24d84962ad3a9c602c663",
      "statement": "An operator can throttle Jev call volume without a release by running `kubectl -n myfeeder set env deploy/myfeeder MYFEEDER_INTEREST_SWEEPBATCHSIZE=20` (relaxed Spring env-var binding on myfeeder.interest.sweep-batch-size), which restarts the pod; once the value is committed into application.yaml and redeployed, the override must be explicitly removed with `kubectl -n myfeeder set env deploy/myfeeder MYFEEDER_INTEREST_SWEEPBATCHSIZE-` because a later Helm upgrade's three-way merge can otherwise leave the out-of-band env var in place.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://CLAUDE.md#L242-L242",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2792cc3857e708588bbbe94a695c3f120984037c59b9c4b418be1c7966aa998a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_5cd5923989994c07b867badad69f0e53",
      "statement": "An emergency stop for Jev scoring is achieved by redeploying with MYFEEDER_TYPESAFE_API_KEY unset: TypeSafeConfig's bean still builds successfully but isConfigured() returns false, so both the sweep and on-ingest scoring no-op without crashing the app; deploy.sh and the Helm chart treat this key as an optional secret, warning when absent, and a key-only change rolls the pod via a checksum/secret pod-template annotation.",
      "evidence": [
